  "difficulty_reason": "Supplying the named Reeb-flow, Giroux classification and transverse-action prerequisites leaves a new source-local mechanism that turns an invariant surface of section plus a normal-form potential into a systolic bound. The author derives the Euler-number derivative jump from the solid-torus gluing, proves positivity of the level integral from the differential inequality J-kJprime>0, and closes the sharp inequality for e at least 2 and for e=1 by minimising the auxiliary function g_e. The counted core also constructs glued solid-torus contact forms whose systolic ratio tends to one-half, so sharpness and unattainedness are proved inside the same unit; this is research-level contact dynamics well above qualification topology.",
